A||||11||Superfiero||Blown Head Gasket||||1||
Z||000000||Superfiero||03-25-2000||07:53 PM||||Have an 88 4 banger but want to buy an 88 GT but it has a blown head gasket, guy is asking for $2900.00, how much work is involved in fixing this problem?||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||03-25-2000||07:59 PM||||One of the things you want to consider is how long has it had a blown head gasket? How long has the bottom end been sitting in oil corrupted by water? Why did he blow the gasket? Is the head warped or cracked? Is there further damage to the block? How much are you willing to spend on the engine repairs? Which bank is it on is it the rear (the one closest to you and realtively easy to get to) or is it the front valve head? (The one you can't see.) Are you doing it yourself?<P>Okay thats more than one thing...<P>I would low ball $1000, 88 GT or not. You don't know what your getting into unless hes super honest.  <P>Good luck! Hope you get the super easy fix up Fiero!<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 03-25-2000).]||||reg||2
Z||000002||Superfiero||03-25-2000||08:31 PM||||My intentions are to build the 2.8 motor with rods, pistons, etc.  Plans are swapping out the heads from a 3.4  I didn't want to spend money on putting a V6 into my 4 banger knowing this will probably cost more than just buying a V6 fiero.  After building motor plan on buying a Rotrex supercharger and boosting around 13 pounds, I think a built 2.8 can take it. Have you heard about the supercharger kit from RS Motorsports? <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WKDFIRO:<BR><B>One of the things you want to consider is how long has it had a blown head gasket? How long has the bottom end been sitting in oil corrupted by water? Why did he blow the gasket? Is the head warped or cracked? Is there further damage to the block? How much are you willing to spend on the engine repairs? Which bank is it on is it the rear (the one closest to you and realtively easy to get to) or is it the front valve head? (The one you can't see.) Are you doing it yourself?<P>Okay thats more than one thing...<P>I would low ball $1000, 88 GT or not. You don't know what your getting into unless hes super honest.  <P>Good luck! Hope you get the super easy fix up Fiero!<P>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 03-25-2000).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||lowCG||03-25-2000||10:33 PM||||Well then go ahead.||||reg||3
Z||000004||mshill||03-26-2000||01:45 AM||||My motto... "If you can't drive it home, it isn't worth more than $1000."  <P>Something you cannot drive probably has much more wrong with it than just a head gasket.  If you plan to rework the engine, then you are going to be putting a lot more time and money into it, and $2900 is high to start with.<BR>||||reg||13
Z||000005||fierospeeder||03-26-2000||01:57 AM||||If it was me i wouldn't spend that much for a car that has a bad engine.  <P>For 2900 i can get a scratchless fiero with a decent 2.8 engine.||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo86se||03-26-2000||11:52 AM||||superfiero: 2900 does sound high for an undriveable 88GT. But if you gotta have it, and find yourself thinking about it all the time, GO FOR IT! You'll start dreaming about it in no time, heck, I just woke up from another Fiero searching dream! Crazy old lady in bed with her dog biting me wouldn't tell me where she knew where a Fiero was! DRAT!<BR> <BR>Keep this in mind: a couple years ago I bought a MINT 88 Formula with almost 200K on the odometer. The owner of the used car lot claimed the motor was blown, I happily shelled out $350 for the car and towed it home. After an hours worth of charging the battery, my mechanic and I fired it up for the first time. Barely held an idle. The oil on the dipstick was milky. Blown head gasket. When we started taking it apart, there were no traces of a head gasket at all. I did most of the cleaning myself, it was nasty in there. We put a new Fel-Pro gasket on, measured everything, and reassembled it. Now the Formula's got over 200K on it, and runs very strong. We painted it white and red.<BR>If I remember right, the "friend" rate was $500, know any good mechanics? ||||reg||10
Z||000007||JIM GOOSE||03-28-2000||02:45 PM||||You didnt say how many miles it has on it. I think if it has less than 90k miles and is decent overall and the head gasket is all thats wrong AND you can do the work then maybe 2900 is OK. I paid 6k for a Lotus Europa that wasnt driveable, it would idle and that was it, transaxle was grinding & the man said he had torn up something. This car only had 20k miles and was original throughout, interior,paint etc. I paid 150 to have it hauled from SC back to GA and started to work on it & this cont. for a couple years. I would not trade my experience with that car for any other I have had. I drove it several years to Roebling Road to vintage races & British car meetings and my wife & I went on a 800 mile trip at one point. You simply cannot mess with old cars & fixing them up without investing more money than they are worth but you need to enjoy the experience.||||reg||14
Z||000008||batboy||03-28-2000||06:28 PM||||I've seen lots of "just a blown head gasket" engines turn out to be major problems. If you buy that car, you have to assume the engine is totally shot. I'm like some of the others, it's too much money. Make a $1000 offer, leave your phone number and let that guy sit on it for a couple more weeks and check back later. Chances are that he'll call you sooner or later with a counter offer significantly less than $2900. It would have to be in completely mint condition and have super low miles to be worth nearly 3 grand with a bad engine (in my opinion).||||reg||1
Z||000009||Superfiero||03-28-2000||09:42 PM||||The car has 75,000 miles on it<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||batboy||03-28-2000||10:18 PM||||You have to assume the engine overheated and blew the head gasket (more likely cracked the head) or overheated after it started leaking or both. Lots of things could be warped.||||reg||1
Z||000011||JIM GOOSE||03-29-2000||11:25 AM|||| One or two other things to consider: The 88GT was the last & best FIERO and basically commands a higher price than all others.<BR>How much you are willing to spend on anything depends on how deep your supply of play money is.<BR>More lies are told about old cars than fishing!!!||||reg||3
